music/The Sandpiper Chorus - The Marines.lrc:
[00:00.00]The Marines' Hymn - The Sandpiper Chorus
[00:04.50]From the Halls of Montezuma to the shores of Tripoli,
[00:11.00]We fight our country's battles in the air, on land, and sea;
[00:17.50]First to fight for right and freedom and to keep our honor clean;
[00:24.00]We are proud to claim the title of United States Marine.
[00:32.50]Our flag's unfurled to every breeze from dawn to setting sun;
[00:39.00]We have fought in every clime and place where we could take a gun;
[00:45.50]In the snow of far-off Northern lands and in sunny tropic scenes,
[00:52.00]You will find us always on the job — the United States Marines.
[01:00.50]Here's health to you and to our Corps which we are proud to serve;
[01:07.00]In many a strife we've fought for life and never lost our nerve;
[01:13.50]If the Army and the Navy ever look on Heaven's scenes,
[01:20.50]They will find the streets are guarded by United States Marines!
